CN_ABSTRACT = (
    "摘要：猪肉降价能在多大程度上缓解家庭食品购买成本？本文利用2020—2022年24个省份27638户家庭的583668个活跃家庭月记录，匹配省级食品价格，分析品类价格涨跌的篮子成本效应及家庭购买响应。将2020年食品配置按2022年价格重新计价，平均成本上升相当于八类食品预算的2.97%。猪肉贡献−4.60个百分点，其他肉类贡献0.60个百分点；肉类净抵消非肉类食品成本增加的约@OFFSET@%，仍不足以使平均篮子成本下降。家庭月成本变化的第10与第90百分位分别为−7.29%和11.75%，不同收入档的成本排序还随涨价品类而变化。购买参与修正的近似EASI估计表明，八类食品自价格弹性点估计均为负，其中七类的95%区间位于零以下；其他肉类和食用油的食品支出弹性高于1，蔬菜和水果低于1。食用油购买率从月度33.50%增至年度88.86%，说明采购频率是解释月度响应的重要维度。研究表明，评价食品价格压力需要同时考虑品类间的价格抵消、家庭篮子构成及购买频率，不能仅依据猪肉价格走势判断家庭食品成本。"
)
EN_ABSTRACT = (
    "Abstract: How far do falling pork prices relieve household food costs? We link 583,668 active household-month observations for 27,638 households in 24 Chinese provinces during 2020–2022 to provincial retail prices. Revaluing 2020 food baskets at 2022 prices raises their average cost by 2.97% of the eight-group budget. Pork contributes −4.60 percentage points and other meat contributes 0.60; their net contribution offsets approximately @OFFSET@% of the non-meat increase but does not eliminate it. Basket-cost changes range from −7.29% at the tenth percentile to 11.75% at the ninetieth percentile, and reported income-bracket rankings change across category-price scenarios. A participation-adjusted approximate EASI system provides complementary evidence on purchasing responses conditional on the observed food budget. All eight own-price point estimates are negative, with seven 95% intervals below zero. Food-expenditure elasticities exceed one for other meat and oils and are below one for vegetables and fruit. Oil purchase incidence rises from 33.50% in monthly records to 88.86% in annual records, highlighting the relevance of purchasing frequency to short-run responses. These findings show why cheaper pork need not make the average food basket cheaper and why food-affordability monitoring should account for category-price offsets, basket composition, and purchase timing."
)

